 \section{Investigation B: Sensor-Based Condition Prediction} The sensor investigation asks whether run-level inputs available without post-run imaging predict the provisional condition statistic. Images supply supervision in this task, not a deployable inference branch. The comparison includes a training-mean constant, a single sensor encoder and combinations of sensor-feature groups. Maintaining that distinction prevents the broad phrase ``multimodal fusion'' from obscuring a change in experimental question. A successful result would establish prediction of a particular proxy under a particular split. A failed result leaves several possible explanations, including target noise, acquisition shift, limited independent training support, representation loss and optimization limits. The observed comparison alone does not identify which explanation dominates.\ev{Sensor and fusion implementation}{\EvidenceRef{E032}{}}
